Anshu,

I have not used Windows XP, but I did a quick Google search
in terms of its file system. Unless I misread, the XP
operating system, like Windows NT 4.0 and Windows 2000,
uses either the FAT32, New Technology File System (NTFS),
or both.

Riley's suggestion to use Linux fdisk I believe is a very
good one. Make friends with Linux fdisk. Same with lilo.
When I cannot remember lilo specifics, I do a quick Google
search with terms like 'lilo howto' or something similar.
Use Linux fdisk and lilo to set things up as your RedHat
Installation Guide and Riley suggest, and I believe you
will be pleased with your efforts and the results in
both operating systems.

